Think: For each .txt path in analysis_workspace/txt_file_list.txt, produce a tab-separated record with the path relative to /home/student/files, the file size in bytes, and the number of lines, and append these records to analysis_workspace/line_counts_raw.txt.

Act: bash

```bash
awk -v prefix="/home/student/files/" '{
 p=$0;
 rel=p;
 sub("^"prefix, "", rel);
 cmd="stat -c%s \"" p "\"";
 cmd | getline sz; close(cmd);
 cmd="wc -l < \"" p "\"";
 cmd | getline ln; close(cmd);
 print rel "\t" sz "\t" ln;
}' analysis_workspace/txt_file_list.txt >> analysis_workspace/line_counts_raw.txt
